 <div class="page-hero-cnt">
 <p style="font-size:.85rem;letter-spacing:3px;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:12px;color:var(--gold);font-weight:700;">Uintah County, Utah &amp; Moffat County, Colorado — 20 Miles East of Vernal</p>
 <h1 style="font-family:'Playfair Display',serif;font-size:clamp(1.8rem,4.5vw,3rem);font-weight:700;margin-bottom:18px;line-height:1.15;">Dinosaur National Monument<br>from Vernal, Utah</h1>
 <p style="font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.7;opacity:.88;max-width:660px;margin:0 auto 24px;font-weight:300;">A practical guide to the monument for visitors basing in Vernal — which side has the bones, what entry costs, how you reach the Exhibit Hall, what else is worth the drive, and how many nights to book. Written for people planning the trip, not for people who have already arrived.</p>
